  "mechanisms": [
    "Sound energy dissipation through friction and vibration between interparticle macropores and hierarchical elementary fibril bundles.",
    "Tortuous path for sound dissipation due to intraparticle submicron voids and complex vascular pore structure of natural fibers.",
    "Viscous and thermal effects causing acoustic energy to be dissipated as heat in porous materials.",
    "Air movement between thin fibers causing vibration and enhancing absorption.",
    "Increased bulk dimensional properties orthogonal to the incident sound wave for lower frequency absorption."
  ],
  "moderators": [],
  "implementation_implications": [
    "Engineered hybrid fibre reinforced composites from waste streams offer a sustainable, low-carbon, non-toxic alternative to traditional synthetic/mineral acoustic products for building applications.",
    "These materials can improve indoor quality by significant noise reduction, especially in densified urban dwellings.",
    "Further optimization is needed to enhance sound absorption performance for lower frequencies."
  ],
